Error [jet.InvalidValidateRule]: A `validate` rule must be `check(condition, at: field, "message")`
  --> validate_bad_rule_shape.jet:6:9
    |
  6 |         print("hello")
    |         ^^^^^
 Why: Every statement in a `validate { … }` block is a `check` call — the first argument is the rule's condition, `at:` names the field the failure is reported against, and the last argument is the message text
 Fix: Write: check(<condition>, at: <field>, "<message>")
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0353
